To fix the error in your Rust code, you need to handle errors properly when making a GET request using the `reqwest` library. Here's how you can modify your code:

```rust
use reqwest::Error;

#[tokio::main]
async fn main() -> Result<(), Box<dyn std::error::Error>> {
    let url = "https://api.example.com/data";

    // Make the GET request and handle errors
    let response = client.get(url).send().await?;

    // Check if the response status is success
    if response.status().is_success() {
        let body = response.text().await?;
        println!("Response Body: {}", body);
    } else {
        eprintln!("Error: Received status code {}", response.status());
    }

    Ok(())
}
```

However, since you're using `client.get(url).send().await?`, which is equivalent to `reqwest::get(url).await?` in the example provided by the model, you can simply use the following code:

```rust
use reqwest::Error;

#[tokio::main]
async fn main() -> Result<(), Box<dyn std::error::Error>> {
    let url = "https://api.example.com/data";

    // Make the GET request and handle errors
    let response = client.get(url).send().await?;

    // Check if the response status is success
    if response.status().is_success() {
        let body = response.text().await?;
        println!("Response Body: {}", body);
    } else {
