To get the values of 'guid' and 'title', we can use a programming language like Python or JavaScript to parse the JSON object. Here's an example in both languages:

### Python Example
```python
import json

# Sample JSON data
data = '''
{
  "node": {
    "hasChildren": true,
    "self": {
      "guid": "G2",
      "title": "Seller Central Help"
    }
  }
}
'''

# Parse the JSON data
json_data = json.loads(data)

# Extract 'guid' and 'title' from the self object
guid = json_data['node']['self']['guid']
title = json_data['node']['self']['title']

print(f'GUID: {guid}, Title: {title}')
```

### JavaScript Example
```javascript
// Sample JSON data
const data = {
  "node": {
    "hasChildren": true,
    "self": {
      "guid": "G2",
      "title": "Seller Central Help"
    }
  }
};

// Extract 'guid' and 'title' from the self object
const guid = data.node.self.guid;
const title = data.node.self.title;

console.log(`GUID: ${guid}, Title: ${title}`);
```

### Output
Both examples will output:
```
GUID: G2, Title: Seller Central Help
```

You can adapt the code to fit the specific structure of your JSON object and the programming language you are using.

